[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Preamble — Parties and Effective Date",
    "text": "This Assignment and Assumption Agreement (the \"Assignment\") is entered into between COMCELL, INC., a Texas corporation, (\"Comcell\"), and TEXHOMA FIBER, LLC, an Oklahoma limited liability company (\"Texhoma\"), (collectively \"the Parties\") to be effective as of January 1,2014, (the \"Effective Date\"). The parties enter into this Assignment pursuant to that Confidential Settlement Agreement and Complete Release of all Claims (the \"Settlement Agreement\") between Comcell and Community Telephone Company, Inc. (the \"Comcell Parties\") and Texhoma, Hilliary Communications, L.L.C., Edward E. Hilliary, Jr., Douglas Hilliary, Dustin Hilliary, and Michael Hilliary (the \"Texhoma Parties\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "1(a) Assignment and Assumption",
    "text": "a. Assignment and Assumption. Texhoma does hereby assign and transfer unto Comcell, effective as of the Effective Date, all of Texhoma's benefits, obligations and liabilities under the PEG Bandwidth Contract, to have and hold the same. Subject to the provisions of Section l(b) below, Comcell hereby accepts such assignment and transfer and therefore agrees to assume all of Texhoma's benefits, obligations and liabilities under the PEG Bandwidth Contract pursuant to the terms of this Assignment."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "1(b) Pro-rations",
    "text": "b. Pro-rations. The assignment by Texhoma of the rights under the PEG Bandwidth Contract expressly includes any maintenance fee attributable to maintenance performed from and after the Effective Date. As such, the parties agree that each party is entitled to their pro rata share of the maintenance fee paid by PEG for the month in which the Effective Date falls. The party who receives such maintenance fee will remit the other party's pro rata portion of such fee as soon as reasonably practicable after (i) the Effective Date or (ii) the remitting party's receipt of such maintenance fee, whichever comes later."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "1(c) Exclusions",
    "text": "c. Exclusions. The assumption by Comcell of the obligations under the PEG Bandwidth Contract expressly excludes any obligation of Texhoma (or any of the Texhoma Parties) not arising under or incurred in connection with the PEG Bandwidth Contract."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "2(a) No Prior Assignment",
    "text": "a. Texhoma warrants that it has not assigned or conveyed any interest in or to the PEG Bandwidth Contract to any third party."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "2(b) Taxes and Fees",
    "text": "b. Texhoma represents and warrants that it has paid all franchise fees, gross receipts, income, sales, use, excise and any other taxes or fees applicable to the PEG Bandwidth Contract due as of the Effective Date."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "2(c) Defaults and Claims",
    "text": "c. Texhoma warrants that other than the claims asserted by PEG Bandwidth in the Lawsuit, Texhoma has not received notice of any default or claim regarding its performance of any obligation under the PEG Bandwidth Contract."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "2(d) Monthly Maintenance Fees",
    "text": "d. Texhoma represents and warrants that the monthly maintenance fees paid to Texhoma under the PEG Bandwidth Contract as of the Effective Date are $9,399.84."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "3. Indemnification",
    "text": "3. Indemnification. Comcell does hereby agree to indemnify and hold harmless Texhoma from and against any and all claims or damages (including expenses and reasonable attorney's' fees) incurred or suffered by Texhoma resulting from any failure on the part of Comcell to discharge or perform any obligation under, or arising in connection with, the PEG Bandwidth Contract assumed hereunder by Comcell."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "4. Lease of fiber optic facilities",
    "text": "4. Lease of fiber optic facilities. The Parties acknowledge that Texhoma leases from its affiliate Medicine Park Telephone Company (\"Medicine Park\") certain of the fibers used by Texhoma to provide service to PEG Bandwidth as described on Exhibit B, referred to herein as the \"Burkburnett Fibers.\" Texhoma agrees to sublease to Comcell, for the term of the PEG Bandwidth Contract, the six Burkburnett Fibers described on Exhibit B at no monthly charge, to be used by Comcell to provide service to PEG Bandwidth pursuant to the PEG Bandwidth Contract. Texhoma warrants that as of the date of execution of this Assignment and Assumption Agreement, these fibers meet the Lease Fiber Optic Specifications in Exhibit B to the PEG Bandwidth Contract. Texhoma further agrees that during the term of this Sublease, Texhoma shall (i) maintain and repair the Burkburnett Fibers in accordance with the performance and maintenance standards provided in Exhibit B to the Maintenance Agreement between the Parties and (ii) promptly restore service in the event of a service disruption or Outage (as that term is defined in the Maintenance Agreement between the parties) at no charge to Comcell. In the event that Texhoma fails or refuses to maintain or restore the Burkburnett Fibers in accordance with the foregoing sentence, Comcell shall have the right to make the necessary repairs to the Burkburnett Fibers and shall be entitled to reimbursement for its reasonable costs incurred in making such 2 CONFIDENTIAL TEXHOMA_000935 Subject to Protective Order | U.S.D.C. E.D. Tex. Case No. 4:16-CV-815-ALM repairs. At the termination of the PEG Bandwidth Contract, this lease and the right of possession in these fibers shall revert to Texhoma and all obligations of this sublease shall terminate."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "5(a) Successors and Assigns",
    "text": "a. Successors and Assigns. Subject to the provisions hereto, this Assignment shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of and be enforceable by the parties hereto, and, in the case of Comcell, its successors and assigns."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "5(b) Construction",
    "text": "b. Construction. All section headings used herein are for reference and identification purposes only and are not intended to, and shall not under any circumstances, serve to alter, amend, amplify, vary, or limit the express provisions hereof."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "5(b) Invalidity of Provision",
    "text": "In the event that any provision of this Assignment shall, for any reason, be held violative of any applicable law, and so much of said Assignment is held to be unenforceable, then the invalidity of such specific provision herein shall not be held to invalidate any other provision herein which shall remain in full force and effect."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "5(c) Governing Law",
    "text": "c. Governing Law. This Assignment shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Texas."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "5(d) Survival",
    "text": "d. Survival. Each provision of this Assignment clearly intended by its terms to survive the transaction contemplated herein, including any representation, warranty, and agreement to indemnify, shall continue in full force and effect in accordance shall survive execution and delivery of this Assignment and the subsequent consummation of the transactions contemplated herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "5(e) Notices",
    "text": "e. Notices. Any notice required to be given to either party under the terms of this Assignment shall be deemed to be given if provided in writing and (1) delivered in person; (2) received within twenty-four (24) hours after delivery to an agent, such as an overnight or similar delivery service, all delivery services prepaid; or (3) received within seventy-two (72) hours after deposited in the United Sates mail, postage prepaid, and addressed to the address for each party set forth below, or such other address for notice as is hereafter provided in writing by the applicable Party: Comcell: Comcell, Inc. Attn: Cliff Humpert P.O. Box l30 Windthorst, Texas 76389 Texhoma: Texhoma Fiber, LLC Attn: Edward E. Hilliary, Jr. 1 Big Rock Road Medicine Park, Oklahoma 73557"
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "5(e) PEG Notices",
    "text": "The parties agree to cooperate to the extent necessary to provide PEG with Comcell's address to receive notice (as listed above) and to secure PEG's agreement to send Comcell any notice that PEG elects to send pursuant to the PEG Bandwidth Contract. In addition, Texhoma agrees that if 3 CONFIDENTIAL TEXHOMA_000936 Subject to Protective Order | U.S.D.C. E.D. Tex. Case No. 4:16-CV-815-ALM it receives any notice from PEG or any third party pursuant to the PEG Bandwidth Contract or otherwise related to the PEG Bandwidth Contract in any way, Texhoma will send a copy of such notice to Comcell's address to receive notice (as listed above) as soon as practicable after Texhoma receives the same."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "5(f) Further Assurances",
    "text": "f. Further Assurances. Each party agrees to take such further or additional action and execute and deliver to the other party such further or additional instruments, agreements, or other documents as shall be reasonably requested by the other parties in order to complete, assure and/or evidence, or more fully complete, assure and/or evidence, the transactions contemplated or described in this Assignment, or to grant, secure and/or confirm, or more fully grant, secure and/or confirm, the rights and benefits intended to be conferred on each party by the transactions contemplated or described in this Assignment."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "5(g) Complete AgreementlRight to Amend",
    "text": "g. Complete AgreementlRight to Amend. This Assignment is the entire agreement between the Parties with respect to the assignment of the PEG Bandwidth Contract. This Assignment may be amended or modified but only in writing as mutually agreed to by the Parties."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "5(h) No Joint Venture",
    "text": "h. No Joint Venture. Nothing in this Assignment shall be construed to constitute or create a joint venture, partnership or formal business organization of any kind and the rights and obligations of each Party shall be only those expressly stated in this Assignment."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "5(i) Severability",
    "text": "i. Severability. If any provision of this Assignment is invalid or unenforceable under applicable law, said provision shall be ineffective to the extent of such invalidity only, without in any way affecting the remaining provisions of this Assignment and the Parties hereby agree to negotiate in good faith with respect to any such invalid or unenforceable provision to the extent necessary to render it valid and enforceable."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "5(j) Confidentiality",
    "text": "j. Confidentiality. The Parties agree that the terms and conditions contained in this Assignment are confidential and shall not be disclosed to any third party without the written consent of the other Party, except as may be required by law."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "5(k) Non-Waiver",
    "text": "k. Non-Waiver. The failure of either Party to enforce strict performance of any provision of this Assignment shall not be construed as a waiver of its right to assert or rely upon such provision or any other provision of this Assignment."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "5(l) Counterparts",
    "text": "1. Counterparts. This Assignment may be executed in one or more counterparts (including by facsimile or by electronic copy or transmission), each of which will be the binding agreement of the executing party and which, when taken together, shall be deemed to be one and the same instrument."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "5(m) Binding agreement",
    "text": "m. Binding agreement. This Assignment, and all its terms and conditions, are binding on Texhoma Fiber LLC and its successors and assigns, and on Comcell, Inc., and its successors and assigns."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "5(n) Representatives",
    "text": "n. Representatives. The signatories to this Settlement Agreement represent that they have authority to sign in their representative capacities."
  },
